SailPoint IIQ Training Expiration Notification Enhancement
1. Executive overview and presentation objective
The enhancement extends the existing NERC training-expiration notification framework so that the SailPoint IdentityIQ task can dynamically discover training courses approaching expiration, rather than relying on manually maintained course IDs. The configured reminder intervals are 30, 15, and 7 days. The work reuses existing SAP training table and policy rule libraries, identifies the relevant SailPoint identities, evaluates training-dependent entitlements, and supports email preparation through the existing notification template.
The scrum walkthrough should answer Sanjay’s key question: where the training data comes from, how the new rule retrieves it, what each existing library does, and which behavior has been tested. It must distinguish notification from actual entitlement revocation and distinguish validated behavior from remaining scope requirements.
Suggested opening statement
We reviewed the existing NERC training notification framework and enhanced it to discover applicable courses directly from the TRAINING table. The rule finds courses expiring in 30, 15, or 7 days, uses the existing SAP Training Table Rule Library to retrieve affected users, and uses the SAP Training Policy Rule Library to identify their training-dependent entitlements. The enhanced rule has executed successfully through the TEST TaskDefinition in scan-only mode. We are now aligning the final notification eligibility filter with the revocation-enabled entitlement requirement and completing controlled email testing.
