10. Notification vs actual access revocation
The enhanced notification rule discovers courses, looks up users, evaluates possible entitlement impact, and prepares/submits emails when enabled. getAccessLostIfTrainingExpires() only returns a list of entitlements; it does not perform provisioning or entitlement removal. The existence, caller path, scheduling, and effectiveness of a separate training-expiration revocation mechanism remain unverified.
For scrum: say “We have validated notification-related identification and access-impact assessment, not actual access revocation.”
